  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="9dff-ae0a-0bcd-0ef0" name="British and Welsh Kingdoms (Age of Arthur) - List Notes" publicationId="28aa-c13e-b61d-4f3e" hidden="false">
      <description>BRITISH AND WELSH KINGDOMS (The Age of Arthur, pp.36-40). Units of Teulu and Combrogi may have a Leader (+5), Musician (+5) and Standard (+5). Allies are documented only. Run for the Woods: a unit may re-roll any failed Leadership or Break test taken in woods or difficult terrain (even if only partly in it), but a failed test may not be re-rolled more than once.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[British and Welsh Kingdoms - British Kingdoms]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 20%
  THE BRITISH KINGDOMS (400-550). Characters up to 33% (Rex, or a Tiern upgraded to Army General). Common warriors at least 33% (Teulu, Combrogi). Uncommon up to 20% (Pagenses). Allies up to 25% from one list: Scots-Irish (Scotti Raiders and Settlers or Dalriada; Ceithern led by Curadh or Toiseach) or Saxons (Sea Raiders or Early Anglo-Saxon Kingdoms; Geoguth and Duguth led by Atheling or Thegn). Special: Teulu and Combrogi on foot lose Light Infantry status (ordinary heavy infantry, up to +3 rank bonus); mounted Combrogi may exchange ponies for horses (+3).
[British and Welsh Kingdoms - Welsh Kingdoms in the West]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 25%
  THE WELSH KINGDOMS IN THE WEST. Characters up to 33% (Rex, or a Tiern upgraded to Army General). Common warriors at least 33% (Teulu, Combrogi). Uncommon up to 25% (Pagenses). Allies up to 33% from one list: Scots-Irish (Scotti Raiders and Settlers or Dalriada), Saxons (Early Anglo-Saxon Kingdoms or Later Anglian Kingdoms of the Heptarchy) or Romano-British Civitates - Brittany (Milites and Pedyt led by Tribune or Decurio). Special: Teulu, Combrogi and Pagenses have Run for the Woods; foot Teulu/Combrogi may choose thrusting spears (Teulu free, Combrogi +1); Pagenses may use Concealment.
[British and Welsh Kingdoms - Welsh Kingdoms in the North]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 25%
  THE WELSH KINGDOMS IN THE NORTH. Characters up to 33% (Rex, or a Tiern upgraded to Army General). Common warriors at least 33% (Teulu, Combrogi). Uncommon up to 25% (Pagenses). Allies up to 33% from one list: Scots-Irish (Dalriada), Saxons (Early Anglo-Saxon Kingdoms or Later Anglian Kingdoms) or the Picts (Early or Later Southern Pictish Kingdoms; Pictish Warriors led by Mormaer or Champion). Special: Run for the Woods; mounted Combrogi may exchange ponies for horses (+3); Pagenses may use Concealment.
[British and Welsh Kingdoms - Dumnonia and the South-West]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Warriors: at least 33%
  Uncommon Warriors: up to 25%
  DUMNONIA AND THE SOUTH-WEST. Characters up to 25% (no Rex; led by a Tiern upgraded to Army General). Common warriors at least 33% (Teulu, Combrogi). Uncommon up to 25% (Pagenses). Allies up to 25% from one list: Scots-Irish (Scotti Raiders and Settlers), Saxons (Later Saxon Kingdoms of the Heptarchy) or Romano-British Civitates - Brittany (Milites and Pedyt led by 0-1 Tribune or 0-1 Decurio). Special: Run for the Woods; mounted Combrogi may exchange ponies for horses (+3); Pagenses may use Concealment.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
